An Idea for another command:

_Listen_.

This would allow you to get a rough idea of whether a monster is nearby,
or the general location of an invisible monster. quieter/smaller creatures
would be represented by a blob of x's (??) roughly surrounding the monster,
Larger/noisier ones by X's, the blob shifting every turn, 

eg:			xxx		   xx
		      xxxxxx 		  xxxx
		      xxxxxxx  ==>    	xxxxxxxx
		     xxxxxxx		xxxxxx
		       xx		  xxx
 			
      
the nearer the monster is the more focussed the blob. As this would mean
having to rearrange the monster list, the symbols could be #,*,or !

another (related) idea is to use a single grey x/X to represent a dark
creature - that is, one that is in the squares surrounding your torchlight
in a dark room/passageway. This would give players a little warning about what
is ahead.

another related idea is to use a red x/X to represent something seen by
infravision from some distance - ie something that cannot be properly
distinguished. Also fire spells should ruin infravision for a few turns.
cold spells should enhance it.

Possible soln: move Xorns under (E)lemental.
	       move xans,gridbugs to some other insect catagory - ants?
	
